#: ../../../dev/building.rst:4
msgid "Building Syncthing"
msgstr "建置 Syncthing"

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:7
msgid ""
"You probably only need to go through the build process if you are going to "
"do development on Syncthing or if you need to do a special packaging of it. "
"For all other purposes we recommend using the the official binary releases "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:13
msgid "Branches and Tags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:15
msgid ""
"You should base your work on the ``master`` branch when doing your "
"development. This branch is usually what will be going into the next release "
"and always what pull requests should be based on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:19
msgid ""
"If you're looking to build and package a release of Syncthing you should "
"instead use the latest tag (``vX.Y.Z``) as the contents of ``master`` may be "
"unstable and unsuitable for general consumption."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:24
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:26
msgid "Go **1.3** or higher. We recommend the latest version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:27
msgid "Git"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:29
msgid ""
"If you're not already a Go developer, the easiest way to get going is to "
"download the latest version of Go as instructed in http://golang.org/doc/"
"install and ``export GOPATH=~``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:34
msgid ""
"You need to set ``GOPATH`` correctly and the source **must** be checked out "
"into ``$GOPATH/src/github.com/syncthing/syncthing``. The instructions below "
"accomplish this correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:39
msgid ""
"We use Go 1.5+ vendoring for our dependencies. If you are using the build "
"script on Go 1.5 or higher this will just work. If you are building manually "
"on Go 1.5 you need to set ``GO15VENDOREXPERIMENT=1``. If you are building on "
"Go 1.3 or Go 1.4 you need to manually ensure the presence of our "
"dependencies in GOPATH, by ``go get`` or copying from the ``vendor`` "
"directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:47
msgid "Building (Unix)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:49 ../../../dev/building.rst:77
msgid "Install the prerequisites."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:50
msgid "Open a terminal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:52
msgid ""
"# This should output \"go version go1.3\" or higher.\n"
"$ go version\n"
"\n"
"# Go is particular about file locations; use this path unless you know very\n"
"# well what you're doing.\n"
"$ mkdir -p ~/src/github.com/syncthing\n"
"$ cd ~/src/github.com/syncthing\n"
"# Note that if you are building from a source code archive, you need to\n"
"# rename the directory from syncthing-XX.YY.ZZ to syncthing\n"
"$ git clone https://github.com/syncthing/syncthing\n"
"\n"
"# Now we have the source. Time to build!\n"
"$ cd syncthing\n"
"\n"
"# You should be inside ~/src/github.com/syncthing/syncthing right now.\n"
"$ go run build.go"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:71
msgid ""
"Unless something goes wrong, you will have a ``syncthing`` binary built and "
"ready in ``~/src/github.com/syncthing/syncthing/bin``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:75
msgid "Building (Windows)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:78
msgid "Open a ``cmd`` Window::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:80
msgid ""
"# This should output \"go version go1.3\" or higher.\n"
"> go version\n"
"\n"
"# Go is particular about file locations; use this path unless you know very\n"
"# well what you're doing.\n"
"> mkdir c:\\src\\github.com\\syncthing\n"
"> cd c:\\src\\github.com\\syncthing\n"
"# Note that if you are building from a source code archive, you need to\n"
"# rename the directory from syncthing-XX.YY.ZZ to syncthing\n"
"> git clone https://github.com/syncthing/syncthing\n"
"\n"
"# Now we have the source. Time to build!\n"
"> cd syncthing\n"
"> go run build.go"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:95
msgid ""
"Unless something goes wrong, you will have a ``syncthing.exe`` binary built "
"and ready in ``c:\\src\\github.com\\syncthing\\syncthing\\bin``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:99
msgid "Subcommands and Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:101
msgid "The following ``build.go`` subcommands and options exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:103
msgid "``go run build.go install``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:104
msgid ""
"Installs binaries in ``./bin`` (default command, this is what happens when "
"build.go is run without any commands or parameters)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:107
msgid "``go run build.go build``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:108
msgid ""
"Forces a rebuild of the binary to the current directory; similar to "
"``install`` but slower."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:111
msgid "``go run build.go clean``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:112
msgid ""
"Removes build artefacts, guaranteeing a complete rebuild. Use this when "
"switching between normal builds and noupgrade builds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:115
msgid "``go run build.go test``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:116
msgid "Runs the tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:118
msgid "``go run build.go tar``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:119
msgid ""
"Creates a Syncthing tar.gz dist file in the current directory. Assumes a "
"Unixy build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:122
msgid "``go run build.go zip``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:123
msgid ""
"Creates a Syncthing zip dist file in the current directory. Assumes a "
"Windows build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:126
msgid "``go run build.go assets``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:127
msgid "Rebuilds the compiled-in GUI assets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:129
msgid "``go run build.go deps``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:130
msgid "Updates the in-repo dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:132
msgid "``go run build.go xdr``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:133
msgid ""
"Regenerates the XDR en/decoders. Only necessary when the protocol has "
"changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:136
msgid ""
"The options ``-no-upgrade``, ``-goos`` and ``-goarch`` can be given to "
"influence ``install``, ``build``, ``tar`` and ``zip``. Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:139
msgid "``go run build.go -goos linux -goarch 386 tar``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:140
msgid "Builds a tar.gz distribution of Syncthing for linux-386."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:142
msgid "``go run build.go -goos windows -no-upgrade zip``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:143
msgid ""
"Builds a zip distribution of Syncthing for Windows (current architecture) "
"with upgrading disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:146
msgid ""
"Building for a different operating system or architecture than your native "
"one requires Go having been set up for cross compilation. The easiest way to "
"get this right is to use the official Docker image, described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:149
msgid "Building without Git"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:151
msgid ""
"Syncthing can be built perfectly fine from a source tarball of course. If "
"the tarball is from our build server it contains a file called ``RELEASE`` "
"that informs the build system of the version being built. If you're building "
"from a different source package, for example one automatically generated by "
"Github, you must instead pass the ``-version`` flag to ``build.go``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:158
msgid ""
"If you are building something that will be installed as a package (Debian, "
"RPM, ...) you almost certainly want to use ``-no-upgrade`` as well to "
"prevent the built in upgrade system from being activated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:162
msgid "``go run build.go -version v0.10.26 -no-upgrade tar``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:163
msgid ""
"Builds a tar.gz distribution of syncthing for the current OS/arch, tagged as "
"``v0.10.26``, with upgrades disabled."
msgstr ""
